    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d751">

                <pb facs="1037" n="917" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg917"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2754: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President of the Technical Board</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stevens</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-10-02T16:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">October 2,
                                1922—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 3—10:13
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>It seems to be well established that the Moscow envoy extraordinary now in Peking
                    will shortly have a conference with the Chinese Government to dispose of Chinese
                    Eastern Railway between themselves.</p>
                <p>The Chinese Government assuming authority under section 3, Radio Resolution,
                    Washington Conference,<anchor n="94" xml:id="d751-f1"/> has seized Russian radio
                    station at Harbin.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stevens</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
